<Bindings>
    <!--
      The keybinding docs/FLOW.md has described since it was written.

      That document lays out the nightly path as "/warband, Enter, Ctrl+C, or
      keybind bar button" and calls it the sub-two-second loop repeated four to
      ten times an evening. No BINDING_* was ever registered, so the real path
      was five actions — Enter, type the command, Enter, Ctrl+C, Esc — two of
      them chat-line typing, which a stuck chat focus eats.

      One binding, on the toggle rather than on a tab: the window opens on the
      export panel and that is what the key is for. Combat is handled where the
      toggle already handles it — the request queues and fires on
      PLAYER_REGEN_ENABLED — so this needs no protection of its own.

      It is deliberately unbound by default. A binding this addon assigned for
      itself would take a key the player has already given to something else.

      THIS FILE IS NOT LISTED IN WarbandPro.toc, AND MUST NOT BE. The client
      finds Bindings.xml in an addon folder by name and hands it to the
      bindings parser. Listing it in the .toc hands it a second time to the
      general UI parser, which knows Frame and Script and has never heard of
      Binding — so it walks the file rejecting every part of it in turn:

        Unrecognized XML: Binding
        Unrecognized XML attribute: name
        Unrecognized XML attribute: header

      three warnings on every login, and no keybinding registered by that pass.
      The attribute lines are what make this expensive to read: they name real
      attributes and invite you to go and delete them, which is what happened
      twice here before the element line was noticed. `category` went first —
      it was never a Binding attribute and deserved to go — then `header`,
      which is Blizzard's own grouping mechanism and was never the problem.
      An attribute warning from this parser is evidence about nothing except
      which parser ran.

      The Lua half is unaffected either way, because it is Lua:
      BINDING_HEADER_WARBANDPRO and BINDING_NAME_WARBANDPRO_TOGGLE in UI.lua
      are what turn the header and the action into words. Without them the
      panel prints the raw tokens.
    -->
    <Binding name="WARBANDPRO_TOGGLE" header="WARBANDPRO">
        WarbandPro_ToggleFromBinding()
    </Binding>
</Bindings>
